// A pixel panel with drawing primitives everywhere and LVGL layouts where the panel's driver says so
// (trait ui). Colours are 0xRRGGBB on the wire; a mono panel (color mono1) lights a pixel whose colour
// is at least 50 % luminance. Commands are queued to the renderer and never draw inside dispatch; the
// panel is flushed at most every flush_ms. Primitives (clear, text, fill_rect) work on every panel.
// ui_load and ui_set answer UNSUPPORTED where `ui` is false (the C3 OLED's built-in 1-bit renderer);
// on LVGL panels a layout replaces the screen and primitives sent after it draw on top. snapshot and
// snapshot_read read back the framebuffer as drawn (test builds), so an agent sees the real screen and
// compares it with the desktop render of the same commands (T-DISPLAY). An e-paper panel (trait
// epaper; design epaper-e1) keeps two 1-bit frames, what has been drawn and what the glass shows, and
// refreshes only the area where they differ: settle_ms after the last drawing command, at once on
// `refresh`, never during a `hold`. A refresh is partial (only changed pixels move, about 0.4 s), fast
// or full (the whole screen flashes; ghosts are cleared); full_every automatic partials are followed
// by a `clean` refresh. `bitmap` takes 1-bit pixels drawn elsewhere (the hub renders images and HTML),
// on every mono panel.
